This code runs in Node.js 20 with default settings. `fetchUser()` fulfils after 2 seconds, and `fetchPosts()` rejects after 100 ms. What happens?

```js
async function load() {
  const pUser = fetchUser();
  const pPosts = fetchPosts();
  const user = await pUser;
  const posts = await pPosts;
  return { user, posts };
}
load().catch((e) => console.log('caught', e.message));
```

